<%# The app had nowhere to say anything, because until now it never had to: a
    heart fills in place, a playlist says where the song went, and everything
    else is just the music. Last.fm is the first thing that happens somewhere
    else and can go wrong somewhere else, and a listener who was sent to another
    website and back deserves to be told how it went.

    Nothing dismisses this and nothing needs to: a flash lives for one request,
    and the next thing the listener clicks is a Turbo visit that draws the page
    without it. %>
<% if flash.any? %>
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-16 z-50 flex justify-center px-4">
    <% flash.each do |kind, said| %>
      <p role="status"
         class="max-w-md rounded-2xl chrome px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-sm shadow-2xl shadow-black/50 animate-enter
                <%= kind == "alert" ? "text-red-300 ring-1 ring-inset ring-red-400/30" : "text-neutral-100" %>">
        <%= said %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
